WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
South Korea is withdrawing more embassy staff from Ukraine after a prisoner of war disclosure dispute. This is Omni View, episode 211. Malaysia's opposition loses its registration, families prepare to return to a Cape Town neighborhood after apartheid error removals, and Alberta decides on Canada, then markets, a progress watch, and understanding the issue. A Sharjay Defehr, the diplomat who runs an embassy when the ambassador is gone, will remain in Kiev with all consulate

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.500
staff, South Korea's Ministry of Foreign Affairs said, to keep diplomatic communication open

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.380
and protect South Korean nationals. The ministry tied the extra pull-out to Ukraine's

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:45.360
disclosure of the transfer of two captured North Korean soldiers without prior coordination.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:50.800
It said Keeve had not given a constructive response despite multiple channels of communication,

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:55.160
and it pointed to ongoing security risks from airstrikes across Ukraine.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:01:00.240
Under South Korea's constitution, all North Koreans are considered citizens of the Republic

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:00.840
of Korea.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.400
Those who reach its territory and seek to defect are generally allowed to stay.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:11.040
From that legal ground, Ministry spokesperson Park Do-soon said the measure was taken to

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.120
facilitate an amicable resolution and restore trust between the two countries.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.100
That is the strongest case Seoul puts forward.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.960
A calibrated protest meant to repair a relationship with a working embassy channel left in place

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:29.920
so the two governments can still talk. Ukraine has insisted that diplomacy must prevail over emotions,

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.480
and it described the situation as resolved. In Kiev's framing, the matter belongs in the

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:40.960
diplomatic channel, not in a cycle of public grievance, and an apology has already been offered.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:46.880
The disclosure came from President Vladimir Zelensky at the United Nations General Assembly earlier

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:52.560
this month. That appearance prompted Seoul to recall its ambassador and threaten further measures.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:58.360
Foreign Minister Cho Hyun noted that a Ukrainian message included words of apology, but fell

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:03.040
short of the level Seoul had sought. Cho Hyun's own account concedes the apology

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:08.000
language is there. The remaining gap, as Seoul describes it, is whether those words meet

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.380
the standard it asked for. Persistent air strike threats had also complicated staff safety.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:14.740
The ministry said.

00:02:17.288 --> 00:02:23.188
Parikatan National, Malaysia's main opposition coalition, lost its legal registration at the

00:02:23.188 --> 00:02:28.928
registrar of societies, the official body that registers political organizations, 11 days

00:02:28.928 --> 00:02:34.108
before nominations for the Malakas state election. Accusations that Prime Minister Anwar

00:02:34.108 --> 00:02:38.908
Ibrahim's government is using state powers to weaken rivals were reported by the South China

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:44.508
Morning Post. For those critics, a registrar's decision this close to a state poll is not a

00:02:44.508 --> 00:02:49.188
technical cleanup. It is the state deciding whether the main opposition grouping can still

00:02:49.188 --> 00:02:54.188
appear as one force when voters see the ballot. Opposition figures have put particular

00:02:54.188 --> 00:02:58.888
weight on that timing, because the block's electoral identity is now uncertain ahead

00:02:58.888 --> 00:03:04.088
of the November 14th vote. Parikatan National had been the main opposition grouping,

00:03:04.668 --> 00:03:09.228
losing registration directly affects its ability to field candidates under a single banner,

00:03:09.468 --> 00:03:14.148
rather than as separate parties walking into the same contest. The coalition was already

00:03:14.148 --> 00:03:19.448
strange by a dispute between its Islamist component, PAS, and its estranged partner,

00:03:19.648 --> 00:03:20.148
Versatu.

00:03:20.888 --> 00:03:24.608
Those internal fractures continue while the block fights to preserve its structure.

00:03:25.188 --> 00:03:30.488
The Registrar's Act and the PAS Versatu split now sit on the table together, and nominations

00:03:30.488 --> 00:03:34.428
will show what banner, if any, the opposition can still use.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:41.700
Families displaced from Bishops Court during apartheid-era forced removals are scheduled to return

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:47.360
under a cross subsidized housing development. All Africa reported that the project aims to restore

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:53.460
land access lost six decades ago while incorporating mixed income housing. The plan is meant to address

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:59.360
historical restitution and current housing needs in the Cape Town area at the same time. Restitution

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.760
here is not only illegal finding, it is a construction schedule that puts people back on land they were

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:10.640
forced off. Ground up noted that the cross subsidized model will allow lower income families to benefit

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:16.460
alongside market rate units. Lower income households are not waiting for a separate later project.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.020
They are written into the same development as the market rate homes that help pay for it.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.680
That mixes the concrete mechanism for reversing one specific forced removal.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.740
The work is due for completion in 2028.

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:34.221
Alberta rejected a proposal to begin a process toward independence,

00:04:34.721 --> 00:04:37.981
with 76% supporting continued membership in Canada.

00:04:37.981 --> 00:04:43.221
The Guardian noted the result as a clear victory for Prime Minister Mark Carney and supporters

00:04:43.221 --> 00:04:44.281
of national unity.

00:04:44.741 --> 00:04:46.821
The ballot was not a snap opinion poll.

00:04:47.261 --> 00:04:51.901
It was the first formal referendum effort on separation in the province, and it is now

00:04:51.901 --> 00:04:52.301
over.

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:56.441
With more than 1.5 million votes counted, that effort ends.

00:04:57.001 --> 00:05:02.381
Unofficial results from elections Alberta showed close to 24% backing the separation process.

00:05:02.881 --> 00:05:05.941
That share confirms the decisive margin against the measure.

00:05:05.941 --> 00:05:11.281
The count stands as a recorded signal of how the province voted on remaining in the federation.

00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:18.613
Luxury home sales fell approximately 17% in Dubai in the third quarter compared with the

00:05:18.613 --> 00:05:23.513
previous year, according to researcher Night Frank, as the Iran war continued.

00:05:24.013 --> 00:05:28.473
Wealthy international buyers remained active but at lower volumes than the prior peak.

00:05:29.013 --> 00:05:34.253
Bloomberg reported, caution around the ongoing regional conflict is showing up in fewer deals,

00:05:34.253 --> 00:05:39.433
labels, even though demand from some markets has not disappeared. Transaction counts dropped,

00:05:39.833 --> 00:05:44.893
yet average prices in the luxury segment held relatively steady. That pattern points to

00:05:44.893 --> 00:05:50.133
a selective pullback rather than a broad walk away by buyers. The war's persistence has

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:53.593
introduced measurable caution into high-value property decisions.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:06:00.170
U.S. investors increased acquisitions of German industrial and manufacturing companies last

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:07.450
year. They completed 76 acquisitions and investments valued at about $29.5 billion. Nearly

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:13.650
double the 2022 total. Deutschewelle reported. Many family-owned German firms, the Middle

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:19.550
Stand, Germany's specialized industrial backbone, are becoming targets as owners reach retirement

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:25.290
age without successors. US buyers are drawn to specialized technical expertise and to customer

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:31.470
relationships built over decades. As of August 2026, U.S. investors had already reached

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:38.230
$23.9 billion in such deals for the year, according to pitch book data. Notable transactions

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:46.350
included the $5.4 billion sale of EBM papsd to Madison Air and Bane Capital's 51% stake in

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:52.419
Everlands. Saudi Arabia is pushing in the right direction on cardiac care in Nigeria,

00:06:52.419 --> 00:06:56.399
area, opening a medical campaign for patients who need specialized treatment.

00:06:56.979 --> 00:07:02.819
The program is set to perform 108 cardiac procedures, including 28 open heart surgeries

00:07:02.819 --> 00:07:06.519
and 80 catheterization procedures, leadership reported.

00:07:07.299 --> 00:07:12.239
Catheterization here is a diagnostic and treatment method that threads a thin tube into the heart,

00:07:12.739 --> 00:07:16.259
and it sits alongside the open heart operations in the same campaign.

00:07:16.919 --> 00:07:21.919
The effort is a concrete piece of bilateral health cooperation at a time when many Nigerian

00:07:21.919 --> 00:07:27.839
patients face limited access to advanced cardiac treatment at home. It bundles surgical interventions

00:07:27.839 --> 00:07:33.659
and diagnostic catheterizations into one coordinated push, with a published count that can be checked

00:07:33.659 --> 00:07:40.997
against what is actually delivered. Tariq Rahman visited Durgapuja pavilions in Bangladesh also today,

00:07:41.497 --> 00:07:46.577
as the government increased its grant for the Hindu festival from four crore to five crore Taka.

00:07:47.337 --> 00:07:52.817
Japan's MMX spacecraft began its journey to Fobos, a moon of Mars to collect surface

00:07:52.817 --> 00:07:55.617
samples that may clarify how the solar system formed.

00:07:56.894 --> 00:08:01.824
You need to really understand embassy staffing during a dispute as a reversible signaling tool,

00:08:02.244 --> 00:08:04.344
not as a synonym for breaking relations.

00:08:04.904 --> 00:08:09.904
A great deal of coverage treats a smaller mission as a dramatic escalation, as if the flag

00:08:09.904 --> 00:08:10.964
has already come down.

00:08:11.544 --> 00:08:16.624
In ordinary diplomatic practice, cutting staff as a routine, reversible signal that stops

00:08:16.624 --> 00:08:22.024
short of ending relations. When a host country's actions create friction, an unplanned disclosure

00:08:22.024 --> 00:08:27.284
of sensitive information is one classic trigger, the sending state can reduce personnel in

00:08:27.284 --> 00:08:32.904
order to show displeasure. It can do that without closing the post. The standard remaining channel

00:08:32.904 --> 00:08:38.444
is a charge-aid affair, who runs the mission when there is no ambassador on site. That arrangement

00:08:38.444 --> 00:08:43.464
lets both governments keep talking without the public picture of a full ambassador still in residents,

00:08:43.464 --> 00:08:48.984
as if nothing had happened. The same tool has a practical safety use. In a dangerous

00:08:48.984 --> 00:08:53.824
capital, a smaller political staff simply puts fewer people in harm's way, while a

00:08:53.824 --> 00:08:59.404
consular section can still serve citizens who need passports, welfare help, or a way home.

00:08:59.984 --> 00:09:05.524
Calibration is the design, not an accident of wording. A true rupture looks different. The

00:09:05.524 --> 00:09:11.744
embassy shuts, consular work stops, and nationals lose an official door to knock on. A protest

00:09:11.744 --> 00:09:17.684
has drawdown looks like this. Fewer diplomats, Asharjay still listed, and citizen services

00:09:17.684 --> 00:09:23.204
still running. The common misunderstanding is to hear staff withdrawn and conclude relations

00:09:23.204 --> 00:09:28.024
ended. Those are different steps, and they are supposed to be different steps so that

00:09:28.024 --> 00:09:30.404
a dispute can be marked without burning the file.

00:09:32.561 --> 00:09:36.861
Official foreign ministry briefings tend to keep that distinction in the precise nouns

00:09:36.861 --> 00:09:42.521
they use. Secondary accounts often condense those nouns into a single verb, pulled, with

00:09:42.521 --> 00:09:46.101
withdrew, hit back, and the calibration falls out of the sentence.

00:09:47.872 --> 00:09:53.412
When a drawdown is in the news, look up whether a charge A-defear is still named, and whether

00:09:53.412 --> 00:09:56.332
the consular section is still processing work for citizens.

00:09:56.972 --> 00:10:01.772
Put an official ministry briefing beside a secondary news account of the same dispute, and

00:10:01.772 --> 00:10:07.332
notice which words survive the cut, remaining diplomat, consular desk, protest, rupture.

00:10:07.332 --> 00:10:13.170
Here, Melaka nomination papers come due shortly, and that filing deadline is the next hard

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:16.090
date for how Malaysia's opposition will appear on the ballot.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:17.650
That's omnivue.

